# DL / Vision Repo Workflow

When exploring a DL/CV repository:

1. Find actual train, eval, infer, options, trainer, and dataset entrypoints.
2. Map CLI flags, presets, env vars, output directory rules, and checkpoint layout.
3. Identify dataset root contracts, split conventions, and loader backends.
4. Identify where metrics are written and which files are authoritative.
5. Produce the shortest reproducible train / eval / result-inspection commands.

Do not trust README over code. Prefer exact file references and exact command lines.
